0001                               *SYSTEM.AS                                                                    *
0002                               *******************************************************************************
0003                               *                                                                             *
0004                               *                          SYSTEM CONFIGURATION                               *
0005                               *                                                                             *
0006                               * This information must be entered by the user to define the configuration of *
0007                               * the system. These equates are used to define the extents of the MCX11       *
0008                               * system tables. THIS FILE MUST BE THE FILE NAMED IN THE ASSEMBLY COMMAND     *
0009                               * LINE. It may be named anything the user wishes. Remember that AS11 names    *
0010                               * S-Record object file after the first file name encountered in the assembly  *
0011                               * command.                                                                    *
0012                               *                                                                             *
0013                               *******************************************************************************
0014                               *                                                                             *
0015                               *                             APPLICATION EQUATES                             *
0016                               *    (These VALUES should be changed for your application where indicated)    *
0017                               *                                                                             *
0018                               *    DO NOT CHANGE THE SYMBOL NAMES BECAUSE THEY ARE USED THROUGHOUT MCX11    *
0019                               *                                                                             *
0020                               *******************************************************************************
0021                               
0022                               *******************************************************************************
0023                               *                      BASIC CONFIGURATION DATA EQUATES                       *
0024                               *                 These should change for your application                    *
0025                               *******************************************************************************
0026                               
0027 0005                          NTASKS  equ    5                   Number of tasks in system
0028 0002                          NQUEUES equ    2                   Number of queues in system
0029 0008                          NNAMSEM equ    8                   Number of named semaphores in system
0030 0003                          NTIMERS equ    3                   Number of timers in system
0031                               
0032                               *******************************************************************************
0033                               *                            SYSTEM MEMORY EQUATES                            *
0034                               *                 These should change for your application                    *
0035                               *******************************************************************************
0036                               
0037 00ef                          MCXVAR  equ    $EF                 Base RAM address of MCX variables (17 bytes
0038                               *                                   are needed. For example, $ef - $ff)
0039 e000                          MCX11   equ    $E000               Base ROM address for MCX11
0040 00ee                          MCXTABL equ    MCXVAR-1            Base RAM address of MCX system tables
0041                               
0042                               *******************************************************************************
0043                               *                           CLOCK AND PRESET EQUATES                          *
0044                               *                 These should change for your application                    *
0045                               *******************************************************************************
0046                               
0047 1024                          TMSK2   equ    $1024
0048 1025                          TFLG2   equ    TMSK2+1
0049 1026                          PACTL   equ    TFLG2+1
0050 0040                          RTII    equ    $40                 RTI Interrupt enabled, prescale = 00
0051 0002                          RTR     equ    $02                 16.37 ms per TICK @ 8MHz
0052 0040                          RTIF    equ    $40
0053 0003                          TOCK    equ    3                   3 TICKs per TOCK (TOCK = 49.14 ms ~ 20 Hz)
0054                               
0055                               *******************************************************************************
0056                               *                              MCX11  EQUATES                                 *
0057                               *                      (These should not be changed)                          *
0058                               *******************************************************************************
0059                               
0060 0005                          TCBLEN  equ    5                   Length of a Task Control Block
0061 0008                          TIMRLEN equ    8                   Length of a Timer Block
0062 0003                          QHDRLEN equ    3                   Length of a Queue Header
0063                               
0064                               *******************************************************************************
0065                               *                            SYSTEM TABLE EQUATES                             *
0066                               *                      (These should not be changed)                          *
0067                               *******************************************************************************
0068                               
0069 0018                          NT      equ    NTIMERS*TIMRLEN
0070 00d6                          TIMERS  equ    MCXTABL-NT          Base address of timer blocks
0071 0006                          NQ      equ    NQUEUES*QHDRLEN
0072 00d0                          QHDRTBL equ    TIMERS-NQ           Base address of queue headers
0073 0004                          NQS     equ    NQUEUES*2 
0074 00bf                          FLGTBL  equ    QHDRTBL-NNAMSEM-NTASKS-NQS  Base address of semaphores
0075 0019                          NTS     equ    NTASKS*TCBLEN
0076 00a1                          STATLS  equ    FLGTBL-NTS-TCBLEN   Base address of Task Control Blocks (TCB)
0077 00a0                          QBODBAS equ    STATLS-1            Last address of Queue Bodies
0078                               
0079                               *******************************************************************************
0080                               *                   TCB INITIALIZATION DATA BLOCK EQUATES                     *
0081                               *                      (These should not be changed)                          *
0082                               *******************************************************************************
0083                               
0084 0000                          INITST  equ    0                   Task STATE at system initialization
0085 0001                          STRTADR equ    1                   Task starting address
0086 0003                          RSTSP   equ    3                   Base address of task's stack
0087 0005                          TCBADDR equ    5                   Address of task's TCB
0088 0007                          TCBDATL equ    7                   Length of a TCB initialization data block
0089                               
0090                               *******************************************************************************
0091                               *                  QUEUE INITIALIZATION DATA BLOCK EQUATES                    *
0092                               *                      (These should not be changed)                          *
0093                               *******************************************************************************
0094                               
0095 0000                          WIDTH   equ    0                   Width of the queue entry
0096 0001                          DEPTH   equ    1                   Depth of queue (# of entries)
0097 0002                          QHADR   equ    2                   Queue Header address
0098 0004                          QADDR   equ    4                   Address of the Queue Body
0099 0006                          QUEDATL equ    6                   Length of a Queue initialization data block
0100                               
0101                               *******************************************************************************
0102                               *    MCX ESR equates                                                          *
0103                               *******************************************************************************
0104                               
0105 0001                          .wait.   equ   1                   Wait for an event to occur
0106 0002                          .signal. equ   2                   Signal the occurence of an event
0107 0003                          .pend.   equ   3                   Set a semaphore to PENDing state
0108 0004                          .send.   equ   4                   Send a message to a task
0109 0005                          .sendw.  equ   5                   Send a message and wait for response
0110 0006                          .receive. equ   6                  Receive a message 
0111 0007                          .deque.  equ   7                   Dequeue an entery from a FIFO queue
0112 0008                          .enque.  equ   8                   Enqueue an entry into a FIFO queue
0113 0009                          .resume. equ   9                   Resume a suspended task
0114 000a                          .suspend. equ   10                 Suspend a task
0115 000b                          .terminate. equ   11               Terminate a task
0116 000c                          .execute. equ   12                 Execute a task
0117 000d                          .delay.  equ   13                  Delay a task for a period of time
0118 000e                          .timer.  equ   14                  Set up a timer
0119 000f                          .purge.  equ   15                  Purge active timer(s)
0120                               
0121                               *******************************************************************************
0122                               *                                                                             *
0123                               *                 TASK AND QUEUE INITIALIZATION DATA BLOCKS                   *
0124                               *                 These should change for your application                    *
0125                               *                                                                             *
0126                               * The next section contains the initialization data blocks for the TCB's and  *
0127                               * the queues. The user should construct these tables as they define such data *
0128                               * as queue sizes, task starting addresses, and stack sizes.                   *
0129                               *                                                                             *
0130                               *******************************************************************************
0131                               *******************************************************************************
0132                               *                      QUEUE INITIALIZATION DATA BLOCKS                       *
0133                               *                            These must be in ROM                             *
0134                               *              (Do Queue definitions before Task definitions)                 *
0135                               *******************************************************************************
0136                               
0137 e000                                  ORG MCX11
0138                               
0139 e000                          QUEDATA equ    *                   Queue data (This must come first)
0140                               
0141                               *******************************************************************************
0142                               *                 THESE ARE LOCAL SYMBOLS AND CAN BE CHANGED                  *
0143                               *******************************************************************************
0144                               
0145                               
0146 0001                          Q1W     equ    1                   Queue 1 width
0147 0008                          Q1D     equ    8                   Queue 1 depth
0148 0008                          Q1SIZ   equ    Q1W*Q1D             Queue 1 size
0149 0099                          Q1BODY  equ    QBODBAS-Q1SIZ+1     Address of Queue 1 body
0150 00d0                          Q1HDR   equ    QHDRTBL             Address of Queue 1 Header
0151 e000 01 08                            FCB    Q1W,Q1D             WIDTH,DEPTH
0152 e002 00 d0 00 99                      FDB    Q1HDR,Q1BODY        QHADR,QADDR
0153                               
0154 0005                          Q2W     equ    5                   Queue 2 width
0155 0001                          Q2D     equ    1                   Queue 2 depth
0156 0005                          Q2SIZ   equ    Q2W*Q2D             Queue 2 size
0157 0094                          Q2BODY  equ    Q1BODY-Q2SIZ        Address of Queue 2 body
0158 00d3                          Q2HDR   equ    Q1HDR+QHDRLEN       Address of Queue 1 Header
0159 e006 05 01                            FCB    Q2W,Q2D             WIDTH,DEPTH
0160 e008 00 d3 00 94                      FDB    Q2HDR,Q2BODY        QHADR,QADDR
0161                               
0162                               *******************************************************************************
0163 0093                          STKBASE equ    Q2BODY-1            Base address of all stacks. This is defined
0164                               *                                    as the address of the last queue body - 1.
0165                               *******************************************************************************
0166                               
0167                               *******************************************************************************
0168                               *                       TASK INITIALIZATION DATA BLOCKS                       *
0169                               *                                                                             *
0170                               *                (Do Task Definitions after Queue definitions)                *
0171                               *******************************************************************************
0172                               
0173 e00c                          TCBDATA equ    *                   Task data
0174                               
0175                               *******************************************************************************
0176                               *                 THESE ARE LOCAL SYMBOLS AND CAN BE CHANGED                  *
0177                               *******************************************************************************
0178                               * You must define certain information about the tasks in your application.    *
0179                               * The information MUST be supplied in the following sequence:                 *
0180                               *                                                                             *
0181                               *      1. Initial status of the task at Power-up                              *
0182                               *      2. The starting address of the task                                    *
0183                               *      3. The base address of the stack for the task                          *
0184                               *      4. The TCB address of the task (This is redundant but it saves time)   *
0185                               *                                                                             *
0186                               * The TCB address, the base address of the stack, and the stack size can be   *
0187                               * defined through equates and used in the definitions. REMEMBER, If you are   *
0188                               * using an HC11 EVB, you must make the stack size for each task AT LEAST 18   *
0189                               * bytes to accomodate the breakpoint mechanism.                               *
0190                               *                                                                             *
0191                               *                           --- N O T E ---                                   *
0192                               *                                                                             *
0193                               * In normal usage, MCX will have the clock driver as task number 1. That      *
0194                               * it the highest priority task in the system and assures the best timing. You *
0195                               * may change it to another if you wish, but it may not provide accurate time  *
0196                               * measurement if it can be preempted by another task. It is strongly urged    *
0197                               * that you always make task 1 the clock driver if your application is to use  *
0198                               * a time base.                                                                *
0199                               *******************************************************************************
0200                               
0201 00a1                          TASK1   equ    STATLS              Task1 TCB address (Task 1 = CLOCK DRIVER)
0202 0093                          STAK1   equ    STKBASE             Base address of task 1 stack
0203 0012                          STK1SIZ equ    18                  Size of stack for task 1
0204 e00c 00                               FCB    0                   INITST is RUN
0205 e00d e4 89 00 93 00 a1                FDB    clkdrv,STAK1,TASK1  STRTADR,RSTSP,TCBADDR
0206                               
0207 00a6                          TASK2   equ    TASK1+TCBLEN        Task 2 TCB address
0208 0081                          STAK2   equ    STAK1-STK1SIZ       Base address of task 2 stack
0209 0017                          STK2SIZ equ    23                  Size of stack for task 2
0210 e013 00                               FCB    0                   INITST is RUN
0211 e014 00 02 00 81 00 a6                FDB    $0002,STAK2,TASK2   STRTADR,RSTSP,TCBADDR
0212                               
0213 00ab                          TASK3   equ    TASK2+TCBLEN        Task 3 TCB address
0214 006a                          STAK3   equ    STAK2-STK2SIZ       Base address of task 3 stack
0215 0015                          STK3SIZ equ    21                  Stack size for task 3
0216 e01a 01                               FCB    _IDLE               INITST
0217 e01b 00 03 00 6a 00 ab                FDB    $0003,STAK3,TASK3   STRTADR,RSTSP,TCBADDR
0218                               
0219 00b0                          TASK4   equ    TASK3+TCBLEN        Task 4 TCB address
0220 0055                          STAK4   equ    STAK3-STK3SIZ       Base address of task 4 stack
0221 0012                          STK4SIZ equ    18                  Stack size for task 4
0222 e021 01                               FCB    _IDLE               INITST
0223 e022 00 04 00 55 00 b0                FDB    $0004,STAK4,TASK4   STRTADR,RSTSP,TCBADDR
0224                               
0225 00b5                          TASK5   equ    TASK4+TCBLEN        Task 5 TCB address
0226 0043                          STAK5   equ    STAK4-STK4SIZ       Base address of task 5 stack
0227 0012                          STK5SIZ equ    18                  Stack size for task 5
0228 e028 01                               FCB    _IDLE               INITST
0229 e029 00 05 00 43 00 b5                FDB    $0005,STAK5,TASK5   STRTADR,RSTSP,TCBADDR
0230                               
0231                               *******************************************************************************
0232                               * Now that the tasks are all defined, all that is left is the definition of   *
0233                               * the base address of the system stack. It should be located 18 bytes below   *
0234                               * the top of the stack area for the last task defined above. The 18 bytes are *
0235                               * there for the stack for the null task.                                      *
0236                               *******************************************************************************
0237                               
0238 001f                          SYSTACK equ    STAK5-STK5SIZ-18    Base address of system stack.
0239                               
0240                               *******************************************************************************
0241                               *******************************************************************************
0242                               *******************************************************************************
0243                               
0244 e02f 20 fe              [ 3 ] nulltsk bra    *                   This is the null task. It is always runnable
0245                               *                                    and always interruptable. It does nothing
0246                               *                                    except provide an active task for the
0247                               *                                    Dispatcher when all other tasks are busy.
0248                               *                                  You may change this any way you wish as long
0249                               *                                    it is never put into a non-ready state.
0250                               
0251                               *******************************************************************************
0252                               *******************************************************************************
0253                               *******************************************************************************
0254                               *                                                                             *
0255                               *                            MCX11 INITIALIZATION                             *
0256                               *                                                                             *
0257                               * This is the MCX11 Initialization routine in which all of the 68HC11 RAM and *
0258                               * internal registers get initialized. This routine is entered upon a Power On *
0259                               * RESET; therefore the first 64 cycles must be spent initializing those areas *
0260                               * of the 68HC11 control register space which must be set up during that brief *
0261                               * period. Then all of the system tables must be set to their initial content. *
0262                               * The user should also include any initialization operatons unique to his own *
0263                               * application. Upon completion, the routine should jump to the start of the   *
0264                               * MCX11 Dispatcher at lable "dispch".                                         *
0265                               *                                                                             *
0266                               *******************************************************************************
0267                               
0268                               *******************************************************************************
0269                               *     Put the special startup code here which must be done within the first   *
0270                               *     64 cycles after Power-on/Reset & set up the internal registers with     *
0271                               *     respect to the application requirements.                                *
0272                               *******************************************************************************
0273                               
0274 e031                          mcxinit equ    *                   This is MCX11 entry point
0275 e031 8e 00 1f           [ 3 ]         lds    #SYSTACK
0276 e034 86 40              [ 2 ]         ldaa   #RTII
0277 e036 b7 10 24           [ 4 ]         staa   TMSK2               Enable RTI Interrupt
0278 e039 86 02              [ 2 ]         ldaa   #RTR
0279 e03b b7 10 26           [ 4 ]         staa   PACTL               Set up RTI clock rate
0280                               
0281                               *******************************************************************************
0282                               *                                                                             *
0283                               * The following instruction is included for use with an EVM board. If you are *
0284                               * going to want to initialize the EVM in such a manner that the MPU will use  *
0285                               * the first 64 cycles to initialize the control registers, leave this one     *
0286                               * instruction in place and perform the following startup procedure:           *
0287                               *                                                                             *
0288                               *            1. Press the USER RESET button on EVM board.
0289                               *            2. Press ABORT SWITCH on EVM board.
0290                               *            3. Ignore any ERROR MESSAGE from the EVM and press ENTER on your *
0291                               *               debug console's keyboard. This should show the Register set.  *
0292                               *            4. Change the content of Stack Pointer Register to legal value   *
0293                               *            5. Start the program with a G command at the address of 'mcxgo'. *
0294                               *                                                                             *
0295                               * If this is not used on an EVM board, and a normal RESET sequence is desired *
0296                               * simply remove the following instruction.
0297                               *                                                                             *
0298                               *******************************************************************************
0299                               
0300 e03e 20 fe              [ 3 ]         bra     *                  Just wait for the ABORT.
0301                               
0302                               *******************************************************************************
0303                               * The second job in the initialization process is to link all of the system   *
0304                               * timer blocks. The address of the first timer block is stored in the word    *
0305                               * in RAM labled "FREE". The word labled "ACTIVE" is set to a 0.               *
0306                               *******************************************************************************
0307                               
0308 e040 86 03              [ 2 ] mcxgo   ldaa   #TOCK
0309 e042 b7 00 ef           [ 4 ]         staa   tickcnt             Set up Tick counter
0310 e045 18 ce 00 03        [ 4 ]         ldy    #NTIMERS            Set up counter for the number of timers
0311 e049 cc 00 d6           [ 3 ]         ldd    #TIMERS             Get address of Timer Blocks
0312 e04c fd 00 f0           [ 5 ]         std    FREE                Store it in the pointer to 1st free block
0313 e04f ce 00 d6           [ 3 ]         ldx    #TIMERS             Set up pointer to 1st Timer Block
0314 e052 18 09              [ 4 ] tmlp    dey                        Decrement timer counter and see if done.
0315 e054 27 09              [ 3 ]         beq    tmdone
0316 e056 c3 00 08           [ 4 ]         addd   #TIMRLEN            If not done, calculate address of next block
0317 e059 ed 00              [ 5 ]         std    0,x                 Store it in link word of current block.
0318 e05b ee 00              [ 5 ]         ldx    0,x                 Then set up pointer to the next block.
0319 e05d 20 f3              [ 3 ]         bra    tmlp
0320 e05f 5f                 [ 2 ] tmdone  clrb
0321 e060 4f                 [ 2 ]         clra                      When done linking the timer blocks, set
0322 e061 ed 00              [ 5 ]         std    0,x                   the link word of the last timer to 0.
0323 e063 fd 00 f2           [ 5 ]         std    ACTIVE              Set up 0 entry for no active timers.
0324                               
0325                               *******************************************************************************
0326                               * The third thing to do during initialization is to set up the queues. The    *
0327                               * queues have a Header and a Body and they are not contiguous. The Queue      *
0328                               * Headers are found immediately below the Timer Blocks in RAM. The Bodies are *
0329                               * found immediately above the Task Control Blocks.                            *
0330                               *******************************************************************************
0331                               
0332 e066 ce 00 d0           [ 3 ]         ldx    #QHDRTBL            Set up pointer to the 1st queue header
0333 e069 6f 00              [ 6 ] qlp     clr    0,x                 Clear next byte in the queue header area.
0334 e06b 08                 [ 3 ]         inx
0335 e06c 8c 00 d6           [ 4 ]         cpx    #TIMERS             See if all queue headers are cleared.
0336 e06f 26 f8              [ 3 ]         bne    qlp                 keep looping until done
0337                               
0338                               *******************************************************************************
0339                               * The fourth function during initialization is to set all of the semaphores   *
0340                               * to a PENDing state. The number of semaphores is equal to the number of the  *
0341                               * named semaphores + the number of tasks + twice the number of queues.        *
0342                               *******************************************************************************
0343                               
0344 e071 86 02              [ 2 ]         ldaa   #NQUEUES            Get the number of queues in system.
0345 e073 48                 [ 2 ]         asla                       Multiply it by 2.
0346 e074 8b 08              [ 2 ]         adda   #NNAMSEM            Add the number of named semaphores
0347 e076 8b 05              [ 2 ]         adda   #NTASKS             Then add the number of tasks.
0348 e078 ce 00 bf           [ 3 ]         ldx    #FLGTBL             Set up pointer to base of the semaphores.
0349 e07b c6 01              [ 2 ]         ldab   #_PEND
0350 e07d e7 00              [ 4 ] smlp    stab   0,x                 Store the PENDing value in the semaphore.
0351 e07f 08                 [ 3 ]         inx
0352 e080 4a                 [ 2 ]         deca                       Decrement the counter
0353 e081 26 fa              [ 3 ]         bne    smlp                Keep looping until all are set to PENDing.
0354                               
0355                               
0356                               *******************************************************************************
0357                               * The fifth thing to do in the initialization is to set up the RAM resident   *
0358                               * portions of the Task Control Blocks (TCB). The TCBs are found immediately   *
0359                               * above the semaphores.                                                       *
0360                               *******************************************************************************
0361                               
0362 e083 18 ce e0 0c        [ 4 ]         ldy    #TCBDATA            Set up pointer to User Defined list of
0363                               *                                    TCB initialization data block.
0364 e087 86 05              [ 2 ]         ldaa   #NTASKS             Set up task counter too.
0365 e089 b7 00 ff           [ 4 ]         staa   notmt
0366 e08c cd ee 05           [ 6 ] tcblp   ldx    TCBADDR,y           Set up a pointer to the TCB.
0367 e08f 6f 03              [ 6 ]         clr    MSGTHRD,x           Clear the message thread.
0368 e091 6f 04              [ 6 ]         clr    MSGTHRD+1,x
0369 e093 18 e6 00           [ 5 ]         ldab   INITST,y            Get the initial status of the task.
0370 e096 e7 00              [ 4 ]         stab   STATE,x             Store it as the status byte of the TCB.
0371 e098 26 14              [ 3 ]         bne    nostart             Branch if task state show it is not ready.
0372 e09a 18 ec 03           [ 6 ]         ldd    RSTSP,y
0373 e09d 83 00 09           [ 4 ]         subd   #9
0374 e0a0 ed 01              [ 5 ]         std    ACTSP,x             Set up pointer to the stack context.
0375 e0a2 8f                 [ 3 ]         xgdx                       Put stacked context address into IX.
0376 e0a3 18 ec 01           [ 6 ]         ldd    STRTADR,y
0377 e0a6 ed 08              [ 5 ]         std    PC+1,x              Put task's starting address into PC word
0378 e0a8 4f                 [ 2 ]         clra                        of the context. Then clear ACCB, ACCA,
0379 e0a9 5f                 [ 2 ]         clrb                        and CCR.
0380 e0aa a7 01              [ 4 ]         staa   CCR+1,x
0381 e0ac ed 02              [ 5 ]         std    ACCB+1,x
0382 e0ae c6 07              [ 2 ] nostart ldab   #TCBDATL
0383 e0b0 18 3a              [ 4 ]         aby                        Bump pointer to next TCB initialization
0384 e0b2 7a 00 ff           [ 6 ]         dec    notmt                data block.
0385 e0b5 26 d5              [ 3 ]         bne    tcblp               Loop until done.
0386                               
0387                               * Now set up the null task
0388                               
0389 e0b7 ce 00 28           [ 3 ]         ldx    #SYSTACK+9
0390 e0ba cc e0 2f           [ 3 ]         ldd    #nulltsk            Get the starting address of the null task.
0391 e0bd ed 08              [ 5 ]         std    PC+1,x              Put task's starting address into PC word
0392 e0bf 6f 01              [ 6 ]         clr    CCR+1,x               of the context. Then clear ACCB, ACCA,
0393 e0c1 6f 02              [ 6 ]         clr    ACCB+1,x              and CCR.
0394 e0c3 6f 03              [ 6 ]         clr    ACCA+1,x
0395 e0c5 cc 00 ba           [ 3 ]         ldd    #NTASKS*TCBLEN+STATLS Get TCB address of the null task
0396 e0c8 8f                 [ 3 ]         xgdx
0397 e0c9 ed 01              [ 5 ]         std    ACTSP,x             Save address of null task's context
0398 e0cb 6f 00              [ 6 ]         clr    STATE,x             Make sure null task is READY.
0399 e0cd 7f 00 fa           [ 6 ]         clr    intlvl              Clear interrupt level.  ** (V1.1 #5) **
0400                                 
0401                               *       jmp    dispch              Start the MCX Dispatcher
0402                               
0403                               *******************************************************************************
0404                               *  The next location should contain the entry point to the Dispatcher.        *
0405                               *  The file "MCX.AS" should follow this file. If not, then you should remove  *
0406                               *  the asterisk on the line above which causes a direct jump to the label of  *
0407                               *  the Dispatcher, "dispch".                                                  *
0408                               *******************************************************************************
0409                               PAGE
0410                               *MCX.AS
