0441                               *  1.1    5/30/89   1. Change calling sequence of .deque. so that the return
0442                               *                      value is in ACCA if entry size is 1 byte.
0443                               *
0444                               *                   2. Changed calling sequence of .enque. so that if the size
0445                               *                      of the entry is 1 byte, it is passed to .enque. in bits
0446                               *                      8-15 of IX. If the size of the entry is 2 bytes, IX8-15
0447                               *                      contains byte 1 while IX0-7 contains byte 2.
0448                               *
0449                               *         11/1/89   3. Corrected incorrect jump destination label in .timer.
0450                               *                       from .pend to dopend
0451                               *
0452                               *                   4. Corrected incorrect branch in .send. causing messages to
0453                               *                      be put into a receiver's mailbox in improper order.
0454                               *
0455                               *                   5. Cleared intlvl during initialization.
0456                               *
0457                               *  1.2    1/12/90   1. Changed the exit logic in .recv. when there is no msg
0458                               *                      waiting in the mailbox. This corrects a problem which
0459                               *                      would leave the task semaphore of the receiver task in
0460                               *                      a WAIT state. Since the .send. ESR does not signal a
0461                               *                      semaphore but simply unblocks the receiving task, it is
0462                               *                      not necessary to manipulate the task's semaphore. The
0463                               *                      original code is deleted and replaced with a simple
0464                               *                      set which backs up the PC and exits.
0465                               *
0466                               *                   2. Moved the code for the backup PC routine and made it an
0467                               *                      internal part of the .deque. function
0468                               *
0469                               *  1.3    3/23/90   1. Disabled interrupts for the endfast routine in isrrtn
0470                               *                      which protects this critical path from being interrupted
0471                               *                      after intlvl is decremented.  If this were to happen
0472                               *                      multiple ISRs could try to restore a task's state.
0473                               *
0474                               *                   2. Removed a hanging push in .signal. that was not poped 
0475                               *                      before returning if the semaphore was not in the wait
0476                               *                      state.  This would only be a problem if an ISR were 
0477                               *                      returning to the Dispatcher or another ISR.
0478                               *
0479                               *                   3. Moved the sei and cli in .signal. to tighten up the 
0480                               *                      critical code and improve interrupt response time.
0481                               *
0482                               *                   4. Moved the sei in .wait. to protect the Critical Code
0483                               *                      there, and deleted the cli since immrtn is CC also.
0484                               *                      This corrects several problems with tasks that wait on 
0485                               *                      semaphores from interrupts.
0486                               *                      NOTE:  to shorten interrupt latency here you might
0487                               *                      move the cli to after setting the wait and then jump
0488                               *                      to endtsk, the tradeoff is another stacked interrupt.
0489                               *
0490                               *                   5. Changed send and receive to use the _RCVWAT status bit
0491                               *                      as was origenally intended instead of _WAIT.  This 
0492                               *                      Corrects the problem where sending a message to a task
0493                               *                      that is waiting on any semaphore causes it to wake up
0494                               *                      as if that semaphore had been signaled.
0495                               *
0496                               *                   6. Added an sei to .deque. to protect some critical code
0497                               *                      in .wait. (see 3 above)
0498                               *
0499                               *                   7. In .enque. moved the loading of IY with queue data to
0500                               *                      later in the routine closer to where it is actualy used.
0501                               *                      This fixes the problem where the backup routine would
0502                               *                      subtract 2 from a word other than the tasks PC which
0503                               *                      was stored on its stack.
0504                               *
0505                               *                   8. Minor things realy, shaved off a clock cycle in dispch's
0506                               *                      tight loop, and used the _PEND symbol in .pend.
0507                               *
0508                               *  1.4    12/7/90   1. Changed cmpb to cmpa in task 5 of TEST.AS. Dequeue was
0509                               *                      changed to return the value in the A accumulator in V1.1.
0510                               *
0511                               *                   2. Fixed a problem with nested interrupt. If you had a
0512                               *                      nested interrupt that did not require a context switch
0513                               *                      followed by an interrupt that did require a context
0514                               *                      switch the stack became corrupted and the system would
0515                               *                      crash. Eliminated endfast routine.
0516                               *
0517                               *                   3. Fixed a problem with purging the timers. Once a timer
0518                               *                      was purged the next timer in the link was not lengthed
0519                               *                      the amount of time of the purged timer.
0520                               *
0521                               *                   4. Fixed a problem with cyclic timers in CLKDRIVER.AS.
0522                               *
0523                               * 1.5      1/24/91  1. Fixed a problem that I introduced in 1.4 in purge of
0524                               *                      timer. Messed with y index register and didn't restore.
0525                               *******************************************************************************
0526                               *******************************************************************************
0527                               
0528                               *       OPT    nol           Remove asterisk if you don't want the listing
0529                               
0530                               *******************************************************************************
0531                               *                                                                             *
0532                               *                             MCX-11 VARIABLES                                *
0533                               *                        (These Will Reside in RAM)                           *
0534                               *                                                                             *
0535                               *******************************************************************************
0536                               
0537                               ************************ Filled in by Initialization **************************
0538 00ef                          tickcnt equ    MCXVAR              Tick counter
0539 00f0                          FREE    equ    tickcnt+1           Address of first free timer block
0540 00f2                          ACTIVE  equ    FREE+2              Address of first active timer in list
0541                               *******************************************************************************
0542                               
0543 00f4                          curtsk  equ    ACTIVE+2            Current task (i.e. the active task)
0544 00f5                          curtcb  equ    curtsk+1            Address of current task's TCB
0545 00f7                          hipri   equ    curtcb+2            Highest priority task ready to run
0546 00f8                          pritcb  equ    hipri+1             Address of TCB of highest priority task
0547                               *                                    ready to run (see hipri)
0548 00fa                          intlvl  equ    pritcb+2            Depth of nested interrupts:
0549                               *                                       = 0 when in a task
0550                               *                                       = >0 when interrupts are nested or 
0551                               *                                         in the kernel
0552 00fb                          temp    equ    intlvl+1            Temporary area
0553 00fd                          width   equ    temp+2              Work area for queue width
0554 00fe                          depth   equ    width+1             Work area for queue depth
0555 00ff                          notmt   equ    depth+1             Work area for queue not empty semaphore
0556                               
0557                               *******************************************************************************
0558                               *                              TASK STATE EQUATES                             *
0559                               *******************************************************************************
0560                               
0561 0080                          _SUSPND equ    $80                 SUSPENDed status
0562 0040                          _WAIT   equ    $40                 WAITing status
0563 0020                          _RCVWAT equ    $20                 Waiting status for message RECEIVE
0564 0001                          _IDLE   equ    $01                 Task IDLE status
0565                               
0566                               *******************************************************************************
0567                               *                             MESSAGE EQUATES                                 *
0568                               *******************************************************************************
0569                               
0570 0000                          MLINK   equ    0                   Message link pointer
0571 0002                          MTASK   equ    2                   Message's sending task
0572 0003                          MSEMA   equ    3                   Message semaphore
0573 0004                          MBODY   equ    4                   Start of message body
0574                               
0575                               *******************************************************************************
0576                               *                          TIMER BLOCK EQUATES                                *
0577                               *******************************************************************************
0578                               
0579 0000                          CLINK   equ    0                   Timer block link pointer
0580 0002                          CTOCKS  equ    2                   Clock tocks in timer
0581 0004                          CRESET  equ    4                   Reset timer
0582 0006                          CTASK   equ    6                   Task waiting on timer
0583 0007                          CSEMA   equ    7                   Semaphore number
0584                               
0585                               *******************************************************************************
0586                               *                          QUEUE HEADER EQUATES                               *
0587                               *******************************************************************************
0588                               
0589 0000                          CURSIZ  equ    0                   Current size of queue (# of entries)
0590 0001                          PIX     equ    1                   Put Index
0591 0002                          QSEMA   equ    2                   Active semaphore: NOTMT or NOTFUL (=NOTMT+1)
0592                               
0593                               *******************************************************************************
0594                               *                                TCB LAYOUT                                   *
0595                               *******************************************************************************
0596                               *
0597 0000                          STATE   equ    0                   Byte 0   Task status:
0598                               *                                     bit 7: Suspended
0599                               *                                     bit 6: Waiting for an event
0600                               *                                     bit 5: Receive wait
0601                               *                                     bit 4: - Reserved -
0602                               *                                     bit 3: - Reserved -
0603                               *                                     bit 2: - Reserved -
0604                               *                                     bit 1: - Reserved -
0605                               *                                     bit 0: Task not in use
0606 0001                          ACTSP   equ    1                   Byte 1-2 Active Stack Pointer for task
0607 0003                          MSGTHRD equ    3                   Byte 3-4 Message thread pointer
0608                               
0609                               *******************************************************************************
0610                               *                            STACK CONTEXT EQUATES                            *
0611                               *         (These values represent offsets from the Top-of-Stack +1)           *
0612                               *******************************************************************************
0613                               
0614 0000                          CCR     equ    0                   Condition Code Register
0615 0001                          ACCB    equ    1                   Accumulator B
0616 0002                          ACCA    equ    2                   Accumulator A
0617 0003                          IX      equ    3                   Index Register X
0618 0003                          IXH     equ    3                   Index Register X (High Byte)
0619 0004                          IXL     equ    4                   Index Register X (Low Byte)
0620 0005                          IY      equ    5                   Index Register Y
0621 0007                          PC      equ    7                   Program Counter
0622                               
0623                               *******************************************************************************
0624                               *                         MISCELLANEOUS EQUATES                               *
0625                               *******************************************************************************
0626                               
0627 0001                          _PEND   equ    1                   PENDing state
